# Character movement
@scenario tutorial_lesson_08
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide thoughtful]
ginger: A move command changes a character's position over time. Watch me cross to the other side.
[if !tutorial_still]
[move ginger rightmark ease_in_out_cubic 740]
[wait 740]
[move ginger rightmark normal exprdur=90]
[endif]
[if tutorial_still]
[show ginger guide thoughtful]
ginger: In reduced motion, I stay here. The next line is the same either way.
[else]
ginger: Here I am on the right. The background stayed still.
[endif]
[if !tutorial_still]
[move ginger guide ease_out_cubic 560]
[wait 560]
[move ginger guide thoughtful exprdur=90]
[endif]
ginger: Change the duration of the first move, then replay it.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: What lets an actor move without replacing the set?
> A new stage preset. -> retry
> A character position. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: Character positions belong to the actor. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Character positions belong to the actor.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_08]
[flag tutorial_done_08]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_2]
